{{also|mull|Mull|müll|múll}}
==German==

===Etymology===
An originally [[Central German|Central]] and [[Low German]] word from {{bor|de|gml|mül||dust}} and {{inh|de|gmh|mülle}}, from {{inh|de|goh|mulli|t=waste, rubbish}}, a nominal formation from {{m|goh|mullen|t=to crush, grind}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*muljaną|t=to crush}} (DWDS).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/mʏl/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Müll.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m,(e)s.sg}}

# [[rubbish]], [[refuse]], [[waste]], [[junk]], [[trash]] (''US''), [[garbage]] (''US'')
# {{lb|de|colloquial}} [[nonsense]]

